  "summary": "Selected evidence records: The terminal CLI is scoped to onboarding, updating, and uninstalling: `super-dev`, `super-dev update`, and `super-dev uninstall`, with `super-dev uninstall --dry-run` offered as a preview of what would be deleted. After onboarding, hosts trigger the pipeline via `/super-dev <request>`, `super-dev: <request>`, or a competition fast mode `/super-dev-seeai`, with the exact trigger varying by host (e.g. Codex CLI uses `$super-dev`).",
